For such purposes the trial court has relied upon following circumstances:-
(i) the deceased met with an unnatural death;
(ii) the death occurred inside the matrimonial house of the deceased;
(iii) false statement was given by the witnesses with regard to illness of the deceased;
(iv) onus under Section 106 of the Evidence Act was not discharged by the accused persons, particularly as they were having special knowledge with regard to the circumstances and manner in which the deceased died on account of poisoning.
